{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/621963-evil-wraiths","id":621963,"title":"Evil Wraiths?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-10T01:59:01-07:00","id":621963,"title":"Evil Wraiths?","content":"I've read a fair few opinions that state that a wraith can easily be &quot;less than saintly&quot; and that shadows don't have to be super negative, &quot;mwahaha&quot; evil types to qualify as a shadow. They can in some bizarre ways desire something logical, even perhaps good, but ultimately that end would likely be self-destructive to the wraith and result in Oblivion claiming them. So I'm asking everyone here for their opinion on the matter. Is it possible to create a wraith that would be &quot;evil&quot; by society's standards, perhaps even murderous, taking sadistic glee in causing harm to others, while the shadow is self-loathing, self-hating, and self-destructive, seeking to bring the evil wraith in question to the ultimate demise \u2014 Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Obviously this would be more suited to an &quot;Evil Chronicle&quot; or as an NPC that PCs would have to track down and fight or something. Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:03:40-07:00","id":622194,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is entirely possible. If, say, a supremacist is using his sick ideology to resist the pull of Oblivion, or a Serial Killer is continuing the murder spree that gave him purpose to do the same*, they are Wraiths. And I'd say a large percentage of Shadows are already of the opinion that Oblivion is all that they (the Psyche and the Shadow) deserve.** The fact that in this case the Wraith is a truly horrible person doesn't really change anything. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind, though, that just because the awful Wraith is getting Pathos from his actions, that doesn't mean he isn't also spreading Angst far and wide. And just because the Shadow might have a legitimate case that the Psyche should be stopped, that doesn't mean it won't work with Spectres and other Shadows to advance the cause of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Admittedly, I'd expect Serial Killers to become Spectres, but it is possible for it to go the other way.<br /> <br /> **As opposed to 'tired of the pain of existence,' or 'want to see the world burn,' motivations other shadows might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:20:30-07:00","id":622228,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not.<br /> <br /> I did something similar for a one-shot at a convention once. The group of PCs were all connected in various ways to a serial killer (including victims, family of victims, police involved in the investigation, etc.) and thus had a lot of overlapping fetters and passions which started coming up when a copy-cat killer started up. One of the PCs (and yes, I know this is pretty horribly cliched, but it was a long time ago, and it was a convention one-shot; nuance is hard) was a &quot;blank slate&quot; ghost that couldn't remember who they were in life, and was rather a complete dick because of having these connections to people, places, and things, they didn't want to care about. Meanwhile, their Shadow was trying its hardest to out this character as the original killer.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily cackling evil vs. moral Shadow, but it worked pretty well. And it didn't even need to be an &quot;evil chronicle,&quot; though that sort of setup doesn't work for longer running games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:40:45-07:00","id":622553,"title":"","content":"Well in Necropolis:Atlanta, there's whole sections of the Wraithly society that are less than good. The Sons of the Dragon that are pretty much the Wraith KKK come to mind. The Iron Legion Anacreon is also noted to be a pedophile, his Passion and linked Shadow Passion on that are particularly awful given the connotation of that. The Penitent Anacreon also wears KKK regalia and whilst quiet and penitent whilst his Psyche is in control, if still somewhat old fashioned on his race views, in Cartharsis he targets mixed race women and assaults and kills them.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Hearse Riders, a vigilante group of youthful wraiths that target and mow down joy-riders. For obvious reasons stated above they're gunning for the Iron Legion Anacreon too. Whilst more heroic (being anti-heroes) than the examples above, they still go out and run people over and kill them in their souped up manifested ghost-hearses.<br /> <br /> None of these are said to be Spectres, though I wonder how Shadow-Eaten the Penitent Anacreon is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:11:17-07:00","id":622592,"title":"","content":"Excellent to read. I was hoping this was the case as I had made a Wraith that was more or less evil. Basically, if it were real, I would <i>never, ever</i> want to meet them. I've given Freudian excuses for this Wraith's behavior and it most certainly is passionate about what it does, but the Shadow would both be ashamed by the Psyche's behavior as well as desiring an end to all the suffering. Oblivion seems like the best route to take as far as it is concerned. The Psyche does have one or two things it would never do, and the Shadow focuses in on that small weak point in the Psyche's armor. &quot;Why not? You do everything else. Is it a reminder of what you used to be like before you became.... <i><b>this?</b></i> Is that a hint of shame I smell? A taste of regret?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Wraith feels that it was unjustly treated in life (spousal abuse among other much more unpleasant things) then striking out and taking joy in the pain of others is how it can regain control over its life. The Shadow will take every opportunity to point out how she is no better than the animal she was married to. That's a roundabout gist of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T23:14:50-07:00","id":623143,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">John Soulis.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T04:42:32-07:00","id":623217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dreamweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/621963-evil-wraiths?p=622592#post622592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent to read. I was hoping this was the case as I had made a Wraith that was more or less evil. Basically, if it were real, I would <i>never, ever</i> want to meet them. I've given Freudian excuses for this Wraith's behavior and it most certainly is passionate about what it does, but the Shadow would both be ashamed by the Psyche's behavior as well as desiring an end to all the suffering. Oblivion seems like the best route to take as far as it is concerned. The Psyche does have one or two things it would never do, and the Shadow focuses in on that small weak point in the Psyche's armor. &quot;Why not? You do everything else. Is it a reminder of what you used to be like before you became.... <i><b>this?</b></i> Is that a hint of shame I smell? A taste of regret?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Wraith feels that it was unjustly treated in life (spousal abuse among other much more unpleasant things) then striking out and taking joy in the pain of others is how it can regain control over its life. The Shadow will take every opportunity to point out how she is no better than the animal she was married to. That's a roundabout gist of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your concept sounds great. The Angry Ghost is a time honored story that fits right into the Wraith setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:55:15-07:00","id":623887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/621963-evil-wraiths?p=623217#post623217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your concept sounds great. The Angry Ghost is a time honored story that fits right into the Wraith setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. It's a little OP in terms of game mechanics, but it is the type that would be sort of &quot;primary villain&quot; material in a chronicle, especially since I figured she would have been dead for a good 70 years, in which time I would imagine a ghost would learn quite a few tricks and gain some power (should they neither succumb to their shadow nor be destroyed or captured by other wraiths).<br /> <br /> What do you think of these as &quot;twisted&quot; passions for a more or less evil Wraith?<br /> <br /> <b>Harm the living (Love)<br /> Be frightening to others (Glee)<br /> Make others rely on me (Greed)<br /> Decorate my home (Vanity)<br /> Punish my husband (Hatred)</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T20:31:19-07:00","id":623900,"title":"","content":"(Just jumping in after posting in another Wraith thread, which in turn reminded me that I hadn't posted in this neck of the forum in a number of years...)<br /> <br /> It's <i>very</i> easy for players/STs to over-simplify the psyche/shadow dynamic, as well as make into an equally oversimplified (and in some cases very incorrect) &quot;good guy/bad buy&quot; scenario. While the psyche generally is more &quot;positive&quot; and the shadow is much more often &quot;negative&quot;, this need not always be the case, as the more underlying truth is that the psyche works towards holding the wraith together (maintaining spiritual integrity... proverbially and literally) while the shadow works towards eventual self-destruction (or, when manifested as a spectre, spread such destruction to as many others as possible). In the case of &quot;evil&quot; wraiths, the shadow may in fact have &quot;positive&quot; aspects that work towards undermining the &quot;evilness&quot; of the wraith in question, disrupting his spiritual integrity. (For a simple example, think of the &quot;evil&quot; of Dexter Morgan, from &quot;Dexter&quot;, vs. the &quot;evil&quot; of Hannibal Lecter -- the former would be a wraith, in this example, while the latter would be a spectre.) It gets really pretty deep in terms of redefining -- and re-perceiving -- what &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; are... literally taking it to a whole new dimension of insight/conceptualization....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T06:08:44-07:00","id":624180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dreamweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/621963-evil-wraiths?p=623887#post623887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you. It's a little OP in terms of game mechanics, but it is the type that would be sort of &quot;primary villain&quot; material in a chronicle, especially since I figured she would have been dead for a good 70 years, in which time I would imagine a ghost would learn quite a few tricks and gain some power (should they neither succumb to their shadow nor be destroyed or captured by other wraiths).<br /> <br /> What do you think of these as &quot;twisted&quot; passions for a more or less evil Wraith?<br /> <br /> <b>Harm the living (Love)<br /> Be frightening to others (Glee)<br /> Make others rely on me (Greed)<br /> Decorate my home (Vanity)<br /> Punish my husband (Hatred)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If you can imagine them keeping the Wraith going rather than giving up in despair, then they are valid passions. So yeah, the ones you listed are workable passions for a wicked Wraith. Hell, individually most of them are fitting passions for a 'typical' Wraith.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how any of them are OP, though. They seem to function much like any other passion, they are just more unpleasant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:20:56-07:00","id":624260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/621963-evil-wraiths?p=624180#post624180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can imagine them keeping the Wraith going rather than giving up in despair, then they are valid passions. So yeah, the ones you listed are workable passions for a wicked Wraith. Hell, individually most of them are fitting passions for a 'typical' Wraith.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how any of them are OP, though. They seem to function much like any other passion, they are just more unpleasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I meant that the Arcanoi and certain other traits that I hadn't listed may or may not be OP, but like I said this is more so a &quot;villain&quot; rather than a straight-up PC. Generally I assign Phantasm, Moliate, Lifeweb, and sometimes Puppetry to the character. You can imagine how she might use these Arcanoi to torment both the living and the dead.<br /> <br /> As for the passions, I appreciate the input and personal opinion. I'm still somewhat new to this and exploring this particular White Wolf world. Good to know I'm at least getting a decent grasp on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}